data-math=\"r^2=8r\\cos\\theta+6r\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=8\\cos\\theta+6\\sin\\theta\\quad\\text{as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.52-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>It is known that the complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|z-1|=|z-\\sqrt3i|\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the locus of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on an Argand diagram.</p></li><li><p>Show that this locus of points can be represented by the polar curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=\\frac12\\operatorname{cosec}\\left(\\theta-\\frac\\pi6\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has midpoint <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac12,\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and perpedicular gradient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2=\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)\\Rightarrow y=\\frac{\\sqrt3}3x-\\frac{\\sqrt3}6+\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\therefore y=\\frac{\\sqrt3}3x+\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/252-p5-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{\\sqrt3}3x+\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r\\sin\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt3}3r\\cos\\theta+\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3r\\sin\\theta-\\sqrt3r\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin(\\theta-\\alpha)=\\sin\\theta\\cos\\alpha-\\cos\\theta\\sin\\alpha\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\alpha=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\alpha=\\sqrt3\\Rightarrow R=\\sqrt{12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=\\arctan\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\\right)=\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\sin\\theta-\\sqrt3r\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> becomes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{12}r\\sin\\left(\\theta-\\frac\\pi6\\right)=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore r=\\frac12\\operatorname{cosec}\\left(\\theta-\\frac\\pi6\\right)\\quad\\text{as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.52-q8","number":8,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the polar curve whose polar equation is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=1+2\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, demonstrating any negative parts using a dashed line.</p></li><li><p>Prove that the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at the points of intersection of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=1+2\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\sqrt3\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are satisfied by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta-\\sqrt3=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q9: Hyperbolic Functions and Hyperbolic Identities</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.52/solutions/assets/diagrams/252-p5-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1+2\\cos2\\theta=\\sqrt3\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1+2(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)=\\sqrt3\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1+4\\cos^2\\theta-2=\\sqrt3\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4\\cos^2\\theta-1=\\sqrt3\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta-\\sqrt3=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.52-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>A line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, intersects the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Find the first two points of intersection between the line and the curve, giving your answers in exact form.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh^2x-\\sinh^2x=1\\Rightarrow1+\\sinh^2x=\\cosh^2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2\\theta}=\\sqrt{\\cosh^2\\theta}=\\cosh\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\sin\\theta=r\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So at the points of intersection: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh\\theta\\sin\\theta=\\cosh\\theta\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh\\theta\\neq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then solve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta=\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\tan\\theta=1\\therefore\\theta=\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{5\\pi}4,\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\\Rightarrow x=r\\cos\\theta=\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\\cos\\frac\\pi4=\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=r\\sin\\theta=\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\\sin\\frac\\pi4=\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\\Rightarrow x=r\\cos\\theta=\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}4=-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=r\\sin\\theta=\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}4=-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4,-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac\\pi4\\right)\\text{ and }\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4,-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cosh\\frac{5\\pi}4\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Or</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}4(e^{\\pi/4}+e^{-\\pi/4}),\\frac{\\sqrt2}4(e^{\\pi/4}+e^{-\\pi/4})\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt2}4(e^{5\\pi/4}+e^{-5\\pi/4}),-\\frac{\\sqrt2}4(e^{5\\pi/4}+e^{-5\\pi/4})\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.52-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has Cartesian equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3-y^3=3xy\\text{ where }x\\leq0\\text{ and }y\\geq0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in Polar form is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\mathrm f(\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi2\\leq\\theta\\leq\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answers in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find an expression for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find the line of symmetry of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its Cartesian form.</p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a loop.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3-y^3=3xy\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^3\\cos^3\\theta-r^3\\sin^3\\theta=3r^2\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^3(\\cos^3\\theta-\\sin^3\\theta)=3r^2\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\theta)=\\frac{3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta}{\\cos^3\\theta-\\sin^3\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)=\\cos\\frac{3\\pi}2\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}2\\sin\\theta=-\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)=\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}2\\cos\\theta-\\cos\\frac{3\\pi}2\\sin\\theta=-\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right) =\\frac{3\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)}{\\cos^3\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)-\\sin^3\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{3(-\\sin\\theta)(-\\cos\\theta)}{(-\\sin\\theta)^3-(-\\cos\\theta)^3}=\\frac{3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta}{-\\sin^3\\theta--\\cos^3\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta}{\\cos^3\\theta-\\sin^3\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)=-\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}2-\\theta\\right)=-\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> this represents <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x,y)\\mapsto(-y,-x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So the line of symmetry is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f\\left(\\frac\\pi2\\right)=\\frac{3\\cos\\frac\\pi2\\sin\\frac\\pi2}{\\cos^3\\frac\\pi2-\\sin^3\\frac\\pi2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\pi)=\\frac{3\\cos\\pi\\sin\\pi}{\\cos^3\\pi-\\sin^3\\pi}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi2\\leq\\theta\\leq\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> it is symmetrical across <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and starts and ends at the origin therefore it must be a loop.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.52-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"13x^2-6\\sqrt3xy+7y^2=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"13\\cos^2\\theta-6\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+7\\sin^2\\theta=10+3\\cos2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Without using Calculus, find the greatest and least distances of points on the curve from the origin.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"13\\cos^2\\theta-6\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+7\\sin^2\\theta =13\\cos^2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta+7\\sin^2\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =13\\cos^2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta+7(1-\\cos^2\\theta)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6\\cos^2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta+7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6\\left(\\frac12+\\frac12\\cos2\\theta\\right)-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta+7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =3+3\\cos2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta+7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =10+3\\cos2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta\\quad\\text{as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"13x^2-6\\sqrt3xy+7y^2=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"13r^2\\cos^2\\theta-6\\sqrt3r^2\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+7r^2\\sin^2\\theta=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^2(13\\cos^2\\theta-6\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+7\\sin^2\\theta)=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^2=\\frac1{13\\cos^2\\theta-6\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+7\\sin^2\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"13\\cos^2\\theta-6\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta+7\\sin^2\\theta=10+3\\cos2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^2=\\frac1{10+3\\cos2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\cos2\\theta-3\\sqrt3\\sin2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and so</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"R\\sin(2\\theta+\\alpha)=R\\sin2\\theta\\cos\\alpha+R\\cos2\\theta\\sin\\alpha\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=\\sqrt{3^2+(3\\sqrt3)^2}=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=\\arctan\\left(\\frac3{3\\sqrt3}\\right)=\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So that</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r^2=\\frac1{10-6\\sin(2\\theta-\\frac\\pi6)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> max and min of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=\\frac1{16}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So the greatest distance is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the least distance is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]}]